<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 60,529 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 60,529 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 60,529 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Monday compared to 51,258 tonnes in the same period on Sunday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Monday	April 27</p>
<p>    Export cargo		 6,912	16,657</p>
<p>    Import cargo		53,617	34,601</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, seven ships sailed and eight berthed. In the next 24 hours, five are expected to sail and 11 are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	Tonnes/TEUs  Ship			Berthing</p>
<p>Crude oil	    55,000	 Capitan Miranda	 28/4</p>
<p>Furnace oil	  25,000	 Al-Safa		   29/4</p>
<p>Lube oil		5,882	 Folice		    30/4</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
